<title>UK: Ex-dividends take 1.219 points off UK's FTSE index.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends take 1.219 points off UK's FTSE index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>FTSE International Ltd said the following FTSE 100 stocks went ex-dividend on Monday taking 1.219 points off the index in early trading today.</p>
<p>			     Dividend in pence  Effect on FTSE</p>
<p>Company		    Net    Gross	 Gross</p>
<p> * British Steel	 7.00     8.75	 1.015</p>
<p> * Energy Group	  5.50     6.88	 0.204</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
